  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 231 AM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThe weather pattern across eastern Idaho will remain generally \nbenign through the workweek, characterized by an absence of \nhigh-impact systems and continued above-normal temperatures. \nEarly morning satellite imagery shows an upper-level shortwave \ntracking well north of the area, leaving a canopy of mid-to-high\nlevel cloudiness streaming across southern Idaho. Regional \nradar returns remain largely negligible, though an isolated \nstray sprinkle or high-elevation mountain flurry cannot be \ncompletely ruled out over the next few hours before dynamic \nsupport exits. Rapid clearing is expected from west to east \nthroughout the day, yielding mostly sunny skies by this \nafternoon.\n\nSkies will remain mostly clear as high pressure rebuilds and \ncenters over the Northern Great Basin from Wednesday through \nFriday. Strong atmospheric subsidence and rising 500 mb heights \nwill promote unseasonably warm afternoons, with daytime highs \nrunning 7 to 12 degrees above seasonal averages. Lower-elevation\nvalleys across the Snake River Plain and Magic Valley will \ncomfortably reach the upper 50s to lower 60s under light, \nterrain-driven winds, making for very pleasant late-autumn \nconditions.\n\nThe tranquil synoptic pattern begins to break down heading into\nthe weekend as an upper-level trough over the Gulf of Alaska \ntaps into Pacific moisture and ejects energy into the Pacific \nNorthwest. The most notable forecast change with this cycle is \nthat models are trending faster and deeper with the incoming \ntrough, bringing an initial intrusion of moisture and cooler air\ninto eastern Idaho late Friday night into Saturday where \nprevious forecast runs were dry. This has resulted in a downward\ntrend in forecast high temperatures for the weekend alongside \nincreasing cloud cover and light shower potential.\n\nA more pronounced pattern shift takes hold to kick off next\nweek. Global deterministic guidance and ensemble clusters are in\nstrong agreement regarding broad upper-level troughing anchoring\nover the western United States. This setup will usher in an\nexpansive cold air mass, making below-normal temperatures\nincreasingly likely along with daily chances for scattered rain\nand mountain snow across eastern Idaho.",
